{"availability":"available","full":"vlasenkoalexey/tpu_performance_autoresearch_wiki","name":"tpu_performance_autoresearch_wiki","description":"Wiki built using Karpathy method containing information about TPU performance optimizations and hooking it up to autoresearch optimization engine","category":"Education","language":"HTML","stars":56,"forks":5,"created":"2026-04-22T17:17:10Z","updated":"2026-09-04T01:07:39Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://vlasenkoalexey.github.io/tags/autoresearch/","topics":["autoresearch","jax","knowledge-graph","llm","machine-learning","mfu","performance-optimization","pytorch-xla","tpu","xla"],"demo":"https://vlasenkoalexey.github.io/tags/autoresearch/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:11.188Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:11.188Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:11.188Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T18:01:11.188Z","stars":56,"forks":5}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Model optimization that feels like cheating. Point an LLM agent at your training script and hardware target, come back to a state-of-the-art-capable configuration with a fully documented research trail.","This repository is an experiment in autonomous TPU model performance optimization, end-to-end: profile analysis, hypothesis generation, experiment execution on real hardware, and result synthesis — all run by an LLM agent against a knowledge base it maintains itself.","The claim is structural, not incremental: given a sufficiently capable LLM, the right profiling tools, and a knowledge base that includes the model's + framework's source, an autonomous agent can drive any (model, hardware) pair to state-of-the-art performance for that combination. This isn't a replacement for performance engineers — it's a force multiplier. The primary goal is unchanged: a faster model. The engineer stays in charge of direction (picking targets, adjudicating contradictions, deciding which gains are worth keeping); the agent absorbs the legwork (reading code, generating…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vlasenkoalexey/tpu_performance_autoresearch_wiki/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9c3f8004a6c0c2140edc8dcd325fc945aadd48cca52df621b77aabab6e76cbed","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:11.352Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:11.352Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Model optimization that feels like cheating. Point an LLM agent at your training script and hardware target, come back to a state-of-the-art-capable configuration with a fully documented research trail.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vlasenkoalexey/tpu_performance_autoresearch_wiki/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Prerequisites (GKE path): authenticated gcloud (gcloud auth login), kubectl, and xpk on PATH, plus a TPU cluster you can reach.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vlasenkoalexey/tpu_performance_autoresearch_wiki/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"9c3f8004a6c0c2140edc8dcd325fc945aadd48cca52df621b77aabab6e76cbed","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vlasenkoalexey/tpu_performance_autoresearch_wiki/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:11.352Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-04T01:07:39Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vlasenkoalexey/tpu_performance_autoresearch_wiki/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:11.355Z","hash":"9c3f8004a6c0c2140edc8dcd325fc945aadd48cca52df621b77aabab6e76cbed","originalBytes":47541,"storedBytes":47541,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["code","model","raw","wiki","tpu","kernel","agent","experiment","run","experiments","llm","xla","every","what","optimization","repo","pallas","framework","kernels","claude","reference","jax","one","xprof-cli","llo","profile","schema.md","get","hlo","runs","tools","under","autoresearch","codex","same","xprof","each","real","back","bash","cloud","dump"